  1	/**
  2	 * Versioning and structural validation for the durable operation document.
  3	 *
  4	 * The operation document is the single source of truth for a durable operation. It is embedded in the task store
  5	 * envelope, whose schema version (`CURRENT_STATE_SCHEMA_VERSION`) governs the envelope only: the envelope gate cannot
  6	 * tell an older operation shape from a newer one. This module owns that second gate.
  7	 *
  8	 * Rules, in the order they are applied on load:
  9	 *
 10	 *   1. A record this build understands (current version) is validated and used as-is.
 11	 *   2. A v1 record (or one that predates the field, which reads as v1) is migrated in memory by adding the schema
 12	 *      version and nothing else. Every v1.1 field is read through a defensive default, so a migrated record keeps
 13	 *      scheduling exactly as it did.
 14	 *   3. A record from a newer build is refused. It is not corrupt: a build that wrote it can still read it, and
 15	 *      quarantining it would destroy evidence. It is also never interpreted as if it were current.
 16	 *
 17	 * Migration is deliberately additive and lossless: the persisted record is re-serialised from the same object, so a
 18	 * reviewer can diff a migrated record against a v1.0.0 one and see only `schemaVersion`. The store writes a
 19	 * `.pre-migration-v1` copy of the whole record before the first v2 write (see `OperationStore.save`).
