499	
500	- When the runner builds `UnitRunContext`, it passes `messages: OperationMessage[]` = undelivered messages addressed
501	  to this unit or to `"*"` (excluding the unit's own), oldest first, capped at 20 per turn.
502	- Those messages are marked `deliveredAt`/`deliveredTo` in the same `save()` that records the unit's `RUNNING`
503	  transition, so a crash cannot deliver twice.
504	- The prompt renders them under a fixed heading (`Messages from other units (advisory; read the referenced artifact
505	  before relying on it):`) with the sender, kind, body and pointers. Control characters are impossible here because
506	  `publishMessage` rejects them at write time, so the prompt is safe by construction rather than by sanitising agent
507	  content (which would corrupt it). Anything that renders a message to a **terminal** goes through `safeTerminal`. On a
508	  **resume**, the undelivered set is re-rendered; a message already delivered is not repeated.
509	- A message is advisory context. It is never verification evidence and MUST NOT change `TurnResult`, the verifier,
510	  or an independence decision.
