   200	A unit skipped because every qualified slot is busy stays `RUNNABLE` and is considered on the next iteration; it MUST
   201	NOT be parked or blocked. If nothing can start while units are `RUNNING`, `decide()` returns `wait` with the reason
   202	"every runnable unit's qualified resource is busy" — never `blocked`.
   203	
   204	`overrideSelection` (operator assignment) is subject to the same reservation rule: an operator-assigned resource
   205	with one slot still runs one unit at a time.
   206	
   207	### 3.5 Failure semantics under concurrency
   208	
   209	| Event | Required behaviour |
   210	|---|---|
   211	| One unit fails while a batch-mate runs | The failure is applied to that unit only; the batch-mate continues to completion; its conversation and state are untouched |
   212	| `signal` aborts | Abort the shared `AbortSignal` to every in-flight unit; await all; apply `cancelled` to each; then `scheduler.cancel()`; persist once per unit |
   213	| Resource exhaustion | Only units requiring the exhausted slot park; unaffected units continue (`scheduler.decide` re-runs after each completion) |
   214	| Crash with N units `RUNNING` | On load, `reconcileIntegrated()` runs first (integrated units become `COMPLETE` from receipts), then `reconcileInterruptedRuns()` applies to the remainder; each gets `+1 unknownResumes` and returns to `RUNNABLE` or blocks at the budget |
   215	| Duplicate completion | `integrate()` is idempotent and returns `ALREADY_INTEGRATED`; a receipt is never appended twice for one unit |
   216	| Scheduler exception | The batch is abandoned; every unit still `RUNNING` is reconciled by the next `run()`; the operation blocks with `NOT_CONVERGING` |
   217	
   218	### 3.6 Verification edges
   219	
   220	An operation MAY declare `implementer → tester → reviewer` with `dependsOn` and `role`. No new mechanism is added:
   275	|---|---|
   276	| `undefined` or `1` | Migrate in memory (§4.3), log nothing, keep `updatedAt`; persisted on the next normal save |
   277	| `2` | Use as-is; validate invariants (§4.4) |
   278	| any other integer | Throw `UnsupportedOperationSchemaError` naming the record's version and the supported version |
   279	| non-integer / negative | The envelope gate already treats the record as corrupt; the operation gate MUST also reject it rather than assume 1 |
   280	
   281	`UnsupportedOperationSchemaError` MUST be a distinct exported class so the CLI can print a one-line message (no
   282	stack) and exit 2, and the view can refuse to render. It MUST NOT quarantine the record: a future-version record is
   283	not corrupt and must remain readable by the build that wrote it.
   284	
   285	### 4.3 Migration v1 → v2
   286	
   287	The migration is **pure and in-memory**; it adds no fields that are not derivable:
   288	
