   486	first, and if every message is undelivered the oldest is dropped with an `OPERATION_MESSAGE_DROPPED` event. This
   487	mirrors the event ring (`scheduler.ts:24,54`) and keeps a long operation's record bounded.
   488	
   489	#### 6.3.2 Producers
   490	
   491	| Producer | Message |
   492	|---|---|
   493	| Unit completion | `artifact` from the unit to `"*"`: its verified summary, plus `refs` to the integration receipt (when git-isolated) and the unit id. Emitted by the runner after `scheduler.apply` succeeds, never before, so an unverified unit publishes nothing. |
   494	| Reviewer verdict | `verdict` from the reviewer to `"*"` when `role === "reviewer"` and the unit completes: `body` is the outcome plus summary |
   495	| Operator | `nexus operation message <op> --from operator --to <unit|\*> --kind <kind> --body <text>` |
   496	| Unit (deferred) | A `send_unit_message` tool. Deferred because it adds a tool surface and an approval-policy effect class; the channel is useful without it, and adding it later is additive. |
   497	
   498	#### 6.3.3 Delivery
   499	
   500	- When the runner builds `UnitRunContext`, it passes `messages: OperationMessage[]` = undelivered messages addressed
   501	  to this unit or to `"*"` (excluding the unit's own), oldest first, capped at 20 per turn.
   502	- Those messages are marked `deliveredAt`/`deliveredTo` in the same `save()` that records the unit's `RUNNING`
