Full-text / keyword / structured search over a XERJ index. Proxies POST /{index}/_search. Pass `prefix` (a `xerj search --prefix` value, resolved by that command) or `index` (a name or pattern) — not both; with neither, searches `ax-*`. Pass `query` as a PLAIN STRING for the definition-first code search (ranks the file that defines a symbol above files that merely mention it — the right default for code), or as an ES query-DSL object (e.g. {"term":{"status":"open"}}, or a bool clause) for structured queries. Omit `query` for match_all. Optional `rerank` adds a second stage that re-judges the top hits with an external relevance model — read that argument's description before using it: it needs a provider the operator configured, and it sends document text off the machine. Optional `judge` re-judges the returned hits LOCALLY (zero tokens, nothing leaves the node) and adds a `_p_relevant` probability per hit — see that argument's description for its honest ceiling. Each hit carries `match_line` when a query term sits in the passage: the absolute 1-based source line of the best-scoring match (a tie takes the earliest line), and `match_lines` for every matched line (capped). Cite `path:match_line`. Both are omitted when no term is located or the passage start line is unknown. `start_line` remains the passage start. Pass `max_tokens` to cap the response at a token budget (never exceeded; see that argument for the tokenizer and the locator-only rule).

exec tool declaration:
